From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wlserver: pass touch through to native Wayland windows

Steam sets one touch click mode for the whole session and turns touch
into pointer input unless a game is known to support touch. That suits
X11 windows, but an xdg-shell window handles wl_touch itself, and pointer
input changes how it behaves: Android under Lepton treats a tap as a
mouse click, which selects a file in the picker instead of opening it.

Pass a touch through when it goes down on an xdg-shell window; X11
windows keep the mode Steam sets. A touch keeps its mode until it ends,
so a focus change in the middle does not split it between the two.

---
diff --git a/src/wlserver.cpp b/src/wlserver.cpp
index 35b6864..484c5c0 100644
--- a/src/wlserver.cpp
+++ b/src/wlserver.cpp
@@ -3856,7 +3856,9 @@ void wlserver_touchmotion( double x, double y, int touch_id, uint32_t time, bool
 		trackpad_dx = tx - wlserver.mouse_surface_cursorx;
 		trackpad_dy = ty - wlserver.mouse_surface_cursory;
 
-		gamescope::TouchClickMode eMode = GetBackend()->GetTouchClickMode();
+		// A touch keeps the mode it went down with.
+		gamescope::TouchClickMode eMode = wlserver.touch_down_ids.count( touch_id ) ?
+			gamescope::TouchClickModes::Passthrough : GetBackend()->GetTouchClickMode();
 
 		if ( eMode == gamescope::TouchClickModes::Passthrough )
 		{
@@ -3962,6 +3964,11 @@ void wlserver_touchdown( double x, double y, int touch_id, uint32_t time, gamesc
 
 		gamescope::TouchClickMode eMode = GetBackend()->GetTouchClickMode();
 
+		// Steam emulates a pointer for X11 windows; an xdg-shell window reads wl_touch itself.
+		if ( eMode != gamescope::TouchClickModes::Disabled &&
+		     get_wl_surface_info( wlserver.mouse_focus_surface )->xdg_surface )
+			eMode = gamescope::TouchClickModes::Passthrough;
+
 		if ( eMode == gamescope::TouchClickModes::Passthrough )
 		{
 			double sx = tx, sy = ty;
